#! ia 1.0

@capability capability-method
  meaning
    says "Work with capability records under the IA methodology: the capability-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a capability. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a capability?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook capability-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook capability-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with capability records, each a grouping of operations, procedures, templates, checks and included capabilities with declared execution bounds: orient through ia position --word capability and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with capability records?"
  subject
    subject-word capability
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word capability at the seat the work concerns, read the capability records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary capability --schema for the sections and fields a capability carries."
      Inference means "Read the capability's playbooks, operations, templates, checks and effects, and find the capability the work belongs to before adding one."
      Decision means "capability is a word of agent-composition-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/agent-composition-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these capability records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the capability must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Compose an existing capability where it fits; a new one names what it composes and the smallest effects it needs."
      Decision means "Extend an existing capability through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the capability will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the capability; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the capability's composition and effects; a capability grants no authority, so the mandate still bounds the work."
      Decision means "Change capability records only through ia preview capability <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Check that every record the capability composes resolves and that its effects match what its procedures do."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the capability, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability agent-profile-method
  meaning
    says "Work with agent-profile records under the IA methodology: the agent-profile-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking an agent-profile. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for an agent-profile?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook agent-profile-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook agent-profile-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with agent-profile records, each a composition of an agent, capabilities, an optional mandate, voice and delegates, and installed execution contracts: orient through ia position --word agent-profile and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with agent-profile records?"
  subject
    subject-word agent-profile
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word agent-profile at the seat the work concerns, read the agent-profile records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary agent-profile --schema for the sections and fields an agent-profile carries."
      Inference means "Read the profile's agent, capabilities, mandate and execution role, and the records it composes."
      Decision means "agent-profile is a word of agent-composition-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/agent-composition-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these agent-profile records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the agent-profile must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Decide which agent, capabilities, mandate and voice the profile composes, and its execution role and limits."
      Decision means "Extend an existing agent-profile through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the agent-profile will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the agent-profile; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the profile's composition and execution; every record it names must already exist."
      Decision means "Change agent-profile records only through ia preview agent-profile <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Resolve each record the profile composes and confirm its role and limits are what the host runs."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the agent-profile, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability execution-binding-method
  meaning
    says "Work with execution-binding records under the IA methodology: the execution-binding-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking an execution-binding. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for an execution-binding?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook execution-binding-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook execution-binding-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with execution-binding records, each a connection from a native target to a host-installed entry or operation descriptor: orient through ia position --word execution-binding and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with execution-binding records?"
  subject
    subject-word execution-binding
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word execution-binding at the seat the work concerns, read the execution-binding records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary execution-binding --schema for the sections and fields an execution-binding carries."
      Inference means "Read the binding's native target and the host entry or operation it connects to."
      Decision means "execution-binding is a word of agent-composition-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/agent-composition-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these execution-binding records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the execution-binding must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Name the target and the host-installed entry it binds; the binding declares the connection and the host installs the entry."
      Decision means "Extend an existing execution-binding through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the execution-binding will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the execution-binding; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the binding with its target and entry; installing the entry stays with the host."
      Decision means "Change execution-binding records only through ia preview execution-binding <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Check that the target resolves and that the host reports the entry installed; a declared binding is not an installed one."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the execution-binding, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability harness-method
  meaning
    says "Work with harness records under the IA methodology: the harness-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a harness. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a harness?"
  composition
