@playbook harness-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with harness records, each a composition of profiles and execution bindings in a workspace under a host contract: orient through ia position --word harness and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with harness records?"
  subject
    subject-word harness
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word harness at the seat the work concerns, read the harness records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary harness --schema for the sections and fields a harness carries."
      Inference means "Read the harness's profiles, execution bindings and host contract."
      Decision means "harness is a word of agent-composition-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/agent-composition-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these harness records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the harness must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Decide which profiles and execution bindings the harness composes, under which host contract."
      Decision means "Extend an existing harness through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the harness will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the harness; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the harness's composition; every profile and binding it names must already exist."
      Decision means "Change harness records only through ia preview harness <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Check that the harness's records resolve, and say which host behaviour remains unobserved."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the harness, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability voice-method
  meaning
    says "Work with voice records under the IA methodology: the voice-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a voice. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a voice?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook voice-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook voice-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with voice records, each communication attributes kept apart from authority and procedure: orient through ia position --word voice and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with voice records?"
  subject
    subject-word voice
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word voice at the seat the work concerns, read the voice records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary voice --schema for the sections and fields a voice carries."
      Inference means "Read the voice's attributes and the profiles that compose it."
      Decision means "voice is a word of agent-composition-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/agent-composition-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these voice records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the voice must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Describe how the participant communicates, apart from what it may do and how it works."
      Decision means "Extend an existing voice through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the voice will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the voice; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the voice's attributes; authority stays in mandates and procedure in playbooks."
      Decision means "Change voice records only through ia preview voice <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Check that the profiles composing the voice still fit it."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the voice, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."
